# XGS Confluence Documentation Standards

**Scope:** Creating or updating Confluence pages under `vecima.atlassian.net` for XGS/XPON design notes, feasibility reports, and technical runbooks.

**Site:** `https://vecima.atlassian.net/wiki`

---

## Language and tone

- **English only** on published Confluence pages — even when the source discussion or draft is in Chinese.
- Do **not** literal-translate section-by-section; **restructure** for an English technical audience (merge redundant clarifications, drop chat-only asides).
- Use clear, complete sentences; avoid telegraphic shorthand.
- No AI or tool attribution in page body or version message.

---

## Required page structure

Every non-trivial page **must** include:

1. **Title (H1)** — descriptive English title matching the page topic.
2. **Scope panel** — one info panel summarizing context, JIRA key(s), and what the page covers.
3. **Table of Contents macro** — immediately after the scope panel, **before** the first major section (`<hr>` or `## 1. …`).
4. **Numbered main sections** — use `<h2>` with `1.`, `2.`, … so the TOC macro can index them.
5. **Last updated footer** — date + brief version note at the bottom.

---

## Table of Contents — use the Confluence macro

**Do not** hand-build a TOC as an HTML/Markdown table with section summaries. Confluence provides a native **Table of Contents** macro that auto-generates clickable links from page headings.

### Placement

```
<h1>Page Title</h1>
<div data-type="panel-info">…scope…</div>
<div data-type="extension" … toc macro …></div>   ← here
<hr />
<h2>1. First Section</h2>
…
```

### MCP HTML format (`updateConfluencePage`, `contentFormat: "html"`)

```html
<div data-type="extension"
     data-extension-key="toc"
     data-extension-type="com.atlassian.confluence.macro.core"
     data-layout="default"
     data-parameters="{&quot;macroParams&quot;:{&quot;style&quot;:{&quot;value&quot;:&quot;none&quot;}},&quot;macroMetadata&quot;:{&quot;macroId&quot;:{&quot;value&quot;:&quot;e5cf62ea-4fd1-444f-aa33-56c0417aae3f&quot;},&quot;schemaVersion&quot;:{&quot;value&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Table of Contents&quot;}}">
</div>
```

- **`style: none`** — plain list (matches current wiki pages).
- The macro reads **`<h2>` / `<h3>` / `<h4>`** on the page; no manual TOC rows to maintain.

### Confluence storage format (REST API direct update)

```xml
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="toc" ac:schema-version="1">
  <ac:parameter ac:name="style">none</ac:parameter>
</ac:structured-macro>
```

### Heading rules (for TOC to work)

- Top-level sections: `<h2>1. Problem Statement</h2>`, `<h2>2. …</h2>`, etc.
- Subsections: `<h3>11.1 …</h3>`, `<h4>…</h4>` — nested under parent in TOC.
- Do **not** use bold paragraphs instead of headings for section titles.

### When editing an existing page

- If a hand-built TOC table is present, **remove it** and insert the TOC macro instead.
- After adding or renaming sections, the macro updates automatically — no TOC table edits needed.

**Reference page:** [Per-PON Indication Parallelization](https://vecima.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~Oreo.Yang/pages/210174587) (v11+).

